  "visualBrief": "Native principal prison exterior with staggered cellhouse wings, attached dining/kitchen and lower southeast administration frontage; nine-bay central arched entrance, two tiers of large recessed metal-grid windows over smaller base lights, plain concrete pilasters, rusticated lower walls, stepped cornices/parapets and narrow roof rods. Three long gabled glazed roof monitors, later solar-panel rows and an integral weathered cylindrical roof cistern with shallow conical cover. Short front entry apron and steps; separate lighthouse, detached cistern terrace, island guard towers/barracks and ruins excluded.",
